  "_meta": {
    "batch": "bool_research_batch_4",
    "date": "2026-07-22",
    "researcher": "agv-spec-researcher",
    "confidence_policy": "true=confirmed official; false=type-rule impossible or documented not-supported; null=unknown/not documented. Never guess.",
    "global_notes": [
      "outdoor_capable set null everywhere: no IP65+/outdoor rating confirmed for any product in this batch (SAFELOG M4 is only IP54, not outdoor; OTTO/Omron/Oceaneering/SEW are indoor logistics robots). Batch legend calling SAFELOG GT1 'outdoor' could NOT be corroborated on OEM/qviro/SYNAOS sources -> left null, not true.",
      "barcode_readers, humidity_control_capable, rack_pin_compatible, trailer_loading, trailer_unloading, stock_line_scanning, busbar_compatible, intersection_management, task_interleaving, onboard_ui, ergonomic_height_adjustable, multi_language_display, gamification: no official source found for any product -> null (except pre-existing Omron LD-130CT humidity_control_capable=true, preserved).",
      "vda5050_compatible for Omron LD/MD/HD set NULL: VDA 5050 is documented for the Omron Mobile Manipulator and via 3rd-party fleet managers (Kinexon/SYNAOS), NOT as a native per-model interface on the standalone AMRs. KO field requires explicit native support.",
      "multi_fleet_capable left null throughout to avoid conflation with vda5050_compatible (distinct field, no independent confirmation).",
      "auto_hitch left null on all tuggers (SEW TV coupling mechanism not documented as automatic)."
    ]
  },
